          "description": "Year 2020, August, hour 7, source type 21, road type 4, county 26161, zone 261610 -- byte for byte `process-tirewear`'s and `process-brakewear`'s scope, so the whole activity half of this fixture is already checked end to end by two others. The RunSpec XML says month 7 and hour 6; the execution database says 8 and 7 and it is the authority (docs/mixed-onroad.md 0.1). The four columns after the temperature are new here: the two humidity columns the NOx correction reads, and the three scope numbers the fuel supply is resolved by.\n\nTHE TWO HUMIDITY ROWS FACE THE REFERENCE ACROSS THIS DOCUMENT'S OWN ARITHMETIC (docs/esm-conventions.md 35.4). Their `expected` is what `ZoneMonthHour` STORES; since docs/meteorology-generator.md 8.2 the value under test is not that column but MG-4 to MG-7 run here from `temperature`, `relHumidity` and `County.barometricPressure`. Measured, the port lands 10.053684062398 against the stored 10.053684293477 (2.2985e-08 relative) and 0.015929058669 against 0.015929059029 (2.2619e-08). Those two rows therefore carry `rel: 1e-7` -- four times the worse of the pair, the gate components/meteorology.esm asserts the whole generator at, and 200x tighter than tolerance.toml's per-cell 2e-05. Every other row here is a key and stays exact.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
