        {
          "id": "the_crankcase_ratio_is_banded_by_model_year_and_its_absence_drops_the_row",
          "description": "`CrankcaseEmissionCalculatorNonPM`'s one lookup, and both halves of it. THE BAND: gasoline is 0.33 to model year 1968 and 0.0132 after, so only the second band is reachable from 1980 and a document that took the first matching row would be 25 times wrong on every gasoline cell; diesel is 0.037 to model year 2000 and EXACTLY 0 from 2001, so both of its bands are live inside this run's window and the 2001 rows are emitted carrying zero. THE KEY: there is no fuelTypeID 9 row at all, so an electricity cohort has no crankcase row -- not a zero, no row -- and that is the difference between 248 and 208 rows per pollutant. The three pollutants' ratios differ by four orders of magnitude (0.0132, 0.00052, 0.00004 on gasoline), so a lookup that lost the pollutant-process key could not pass this.",
