        {
          "id": "the_worked_examples_reach_MOVESOutput_in_both_processes",
          "description": "The end of the chain, against `MOVESOutput` itself, at seventeen of its 1368 rows chosen to cover both processes, all three pollutants, all four fuels on process 1 and all three on process 15, both day types and both ends of the model-year range. `output_rows` is rate-major over the 684 emitting rate rows, one day type each, so output row r is rate rank r. It was 1,368 rows with the two day types INTERLEAVED -- 2r-1 the weekend and 2r the weekday -- which is why the surviving ordinals here are the old even ones halved (docs/esm-conventions.md 42). The SCC is COMPUTED from four columns of the row -- note that its last two digits are the PROCESS, so 2201210401 and 2201210415 are the same vehicle on the two processes and an SCC that lost the process would relabel 624 rows while passing every value check.",
